  "verbalization": "Ganoderic Acid Y is implicated in the biological activity of S1B1-20 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ganoderic Acid Y directly targets LS174T, which is a target of multiple complex compounds, including (1S,4S,5S)-1-methyl-4-propan-2-ylbicyclo[3.1.0]hexan-2-one and (6S)-2-methyl-6-[(2R,3R,5R,8R,9R,10R,12R,13R,14R,17S)-2,3,12-trihydroxy-4,4,8,10,14-pentamethyl-2,3,5,6,7,9,11,12,13,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-17-yl]-6-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2R,3R,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxyhept-1-en-3-one. These compounds, in turn, target S1B1-20, indicating a potential pathway where Ganoderic Acid Y may influence S1B1-20 through a series of intermediate targets. Additionally, LS174T is also a target of Thalicthuberinec, which further supports the notion that Ganoderic Acid Y may interact with S1B1-20 via a chain of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that the relationship between Ganoderic Acid Y and S1B1-20 is mediated through LS174T and its downstream targets, highlighting a possible role in biological signaling or metabolic pathways.",
